{
  "public_base": "b938072205b82d3eac206150a75c52c001e06784",
  "change": "FilterLayerRef::create now sinks the native factory floating GimpItem reference, establishing independent handle ownership before image insertion. The C factory behavior is unchanged.",
  "original_entry": {
    "c_entry": "gimp_filter_layer_new",
    "legacy_site": "app/core/gimpfilterlayer.cpp:1175",
    "cpp_operation": "FilterLayerRef::create",
    "contract_file": "migration/contracts/cpp-c-entry-map.tsv",
    "qualification": "Closes the evidenced typed-factory independent-ownership sub-obligation. No blanket completion of the original 76 entries or separate 31 hooks is claimed."
  },
  "source_rationale": [
    "gimp_item_init explicitly force-floats new items; gimp_filter_layer_new preserves that factory reference.",
    "ObjectRef::adopt stores the floating pointer without sinking; ObjectRef::sink calls g_object_ref_sink.",
    "Image insertion adds container ownership and consumes floating ownership; pre-sinking gives handle and image independent references.",
    "CloneLayerRef::create already uses the same sink pattern."
  ],
